{"name":"Warp & Weft","hex":"#e5d5c9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"warp","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state, quality, or condition of being twisted, physically or mentally:\n The state, quality, or condition of being physically bent or twisted out of shape.\n\n The state, quality, or condition of being deviant from what is right or proper morally or mentally.","The state, quality, or condition of being physically bent or twisted out of shape."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To twist or become twisted, physically or mentally.\n To twist or turn (something) out of shape; to deform.","To twist or turn (something) out of shape; to deform."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warp"},{"term":"weft","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The horizontal threads that are interlaced through the warp in a woven fabric.","The yarn used for the weft; the fill."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of waif."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weft"}],"entries":[{"title":"Warp & Weft","blocks":[{"text":"Warp & Weft is the ninth studio album by American singer-songwriter Laura Veirs. Released on August 19, 2013, in the United States, and August 24, 2013, in Europe, the album was written by Veirs herself and produced by her husband Tucker Martine."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e4/Laura_Veirs_-_Warp_%26_Weft.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warp_%26_Weft"},{"title":"Ampersand","blocks":[{"text":"The ampersand, also known as the and sign, is the logogram &, representing the conjunction \"and\". It originated as a ligature of the word et."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Et_sign.svg/330px-Et_sign.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ampersand"},{"title":"Warp and weft","blocks":[{"text":"In the manufacture of cloth, warp and weft are the two basic components in weaving to transform thread and yarn into textile fabrics. The vertical warp yarns are held stationary in tension on a loom (frame) while the horizontal weft is drawn through the warp thread. In the terminology of weaving, each warp thread is called a warp end; a pick is a single weft thread that crosses the warp thread."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Warp_and_weft_2.jpg/330px-Warp_and_weft_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warp_and_weft"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Pay_and_Display_sign_with_Tironian_et_for_Irish_agus.jpg/500px-Pay_and_Display_sign_with_Tironian_et_for_Irish_agus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Pay_and_Display_sign_with_Tironian_et_for_Irish_agus.jpg/500px-Pay_and_Display_sign_with_Tironian_et_for_Irish_agus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bilingual Irish street sign, with ⁊ used to represent agus (first line) and & used to represent and (second line)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APay_and_Display_sign_with_Tironian_et_for_Irish_agus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Ampersand_Handwriting_3.jpg/120px-Ampersand_Handwriting_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Ampersand_Handwriting_3.jpg/250px-Ampersand_Handwriting_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Ampersand_Handwriting_3.jpg/120px-Ampersand_Handwriting_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th